        "---\n",
        "## **1. Delivery SLA Adherence & Customer Sentiment Decay**\n",
        "\n",
        "### **Context & Approach**\n",
        "Before breaking down shipping corridors or revenue, we need to answer a core operational question: how frequently are promised delivery dates missed, and what does a delay do to customer ratings?\n",
        "\n",
        "To get an accurate count, delivery timestamps are normalized to calendar dates. Because estimated delivery dates only specify the day without an exact hour, comparing raw timestamps flags packages delivered on the promised afternoon as late. Evaluating arrivals strictly at the date level prevents on-time orders from being falsely categorized as SLA breaches."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c3qiYCW93VTF"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "delivered_orders = orders[(orders['order_status'] == 'delivered') & (orders['order_delivered_customer_date'].notnull())].copy()\n",
        "print(f\"Delivered Orders with valid delivery date: {len(delivered_orders):,} rows\")"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "FRuvD6NWN0Ro",
        "outputId": "97da9c9b-de45-414a-86ed-2962b74b4bc8"
      },
      "execution_count": 9,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
