        "**Key Insights: Delay Severity & Rating Decay Breakdown**\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Early Arrivals Have Diminishing Returns:** Delivering over 3 days ahead keeps average ratings high at 4.30★, while deliveries arriving right on the cusp (0–3 days early) settle at 4.11★. Beating the estimate early preserves customer goodwill, but doesn't meaningfully improve ratings beyond baseline satisfaction.\n",
        "* **The 1–3 Day Buffer Zone:** Mild delays shave ratings down to 3.29★, with 1-star ratings climbing to 24.9%. While negative feedback increases, customer sentiment hasn't completely turned negative yet.\n",
        "* **The 4-Day Tipping Point:** Crossing into 4–7 days late causes ratings to crater to 2.10★, with 56.8% of feedback turning into 1-star reviews. This is the critical threshold where buyers clearly lose patience.\n",
        "* **Severe Delays (>7 Days):** Extended delays result in near-total review failure: an average score of 1.70★ and 67.9% 1-star reviews. Nearly 7 out of 10 customers leaving feedback on these orders write off the experience entirely."
