      "source": [
        "**Key Insights: Regional Freight Burden & Service Disconnect**\n",
        "\n",
        "* **The Remote Region Cost Penalty:** Customers in the North and Northeast bear the heaviest logistics friction. Average freight fees in the North reach R\\$ 41.3 with a 22.6-day transit time, while the Northeast averages R\\$ 36.0 over 20.0 days. This is more than double the cost and duration seen in the Southeast (R\\$ 19.8 over 10.8 days).\n",
        "* **Elevated Freight Burden in Outer Regions:** In the North and Northeast, shipping fees make up 22.7% and 21.7% of total merchandise value, respectively. By comparison, Southeast buyers face a freight burden of just 15.2%.\n",
        "* **Compounded Frustration Drags Customer Ratings:** The combination of prolonged delivery windows and high freight overhead directly depresses customer sentiment. The Northeast records the lowest regional rating across the platform at 3.97★, followed by the North at 4.03★, whereas regions with sub-15 day transit times maintain ratings above 4.13★."
      ],
