      "source": [
        "**Key Insights: Freight Burden vs Transit Time and Sentiment**\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Order Share Across Burden Tiers:** Over 64% of platform orders carry moderate or low shipping costs (30.2% at <= 15% of item price, 34.7% at 15–30%). However, 15.8% of orders fall into the extreme tier where shipping fees exceed half the item's value.\n",
        "* **Transit Time Correlates With Freight Ratio:** Average delivery time rises steadily from roughly 11.7 days for low-burden items to nearly 14 days for the extreme burden group.\n",
        "* **Freight Alone Does Not Drop Review Scores:** Despite delivery taking longer and shipping costs making up a higher percentage of the purchase, the average review score stays flat between 4.1★ and 4.2★ across every tier. This suggests shipping cost on its own is not what drives reviews, though regions differ in both freight and delivery time, so it is only a rough picture.\n",
        "* **Within-Region Check:** Comparing orders inside the same region, late rates and review scores barely change across freight tiers (review scores stay within about 0.1★ in every region, with no consistent pattern in late rates). The slightly worse numbers for high-burden tiers in the overall view come mostly from regional mix, since the extreme tier has more Northeast orders. This supports the finding that freight cost is not what drives reviews."
