        "\n",
        "### **What the Data Shows**\n",
        "* **1 in 15 orders (6.77%) breaches SLA:** Delayed orders experience a steep rating drop, averaging 2.27★ compared to 4.29★ for on-time deliveries.\n",
        "* **Sentiment decay accelerates by day 4:** Delays of 1–3 days drop average ratings to 3.29★, but severe delays (>7 days) crater satisfaction down to 1.70★, with nearly 68% of customers leaving 1-star reviews.\n",
        "* **Geographic concentration:** Northeast corridors suffer the highest breach rates (e.g., Southeast to Northeast at 12.89% late). São Paulo has the most late orders (1,820) simply because of its size, but only at a 4.49% late rate. Rio de Janeiro (RJ) is second with 1,495 late orders at 12.11%, about 2.7 times São Paulo's rate.\n",
        "* **Freight cost does not appear to explain bad reviews:** freight value and burden ratio show near-zero correlation with review scores, and the pattern holds within each region. Late deliveries are tied to low ratings far more strongly than shipping fees are.\n",
        "* **Financial exposure:** Delayed deliveries account for R\\$ 985,924.34 in product GMV (7.46% of platform total), with 45.4% of that at-risk revenue concentrated in orders delayed past a full week.\n",
